digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56815-9
  rankdir="TB";
  "I2" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: Given vdW surface lacks dangling bonds and causes poor nucleation, therefore conventional dielectric integration is a bottleneck."];
  "I3" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: Given transfer technique loosens restrictions and nanogap suppresses leakage, therefore transfer enables high-quality dielectric integration."];
  "I5" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-reasoning: Given gas-to-solid is limited and wet chemistry is versatile, therefore wet chemistry offers superior functional diversity."];
  "N1" [label="(1,0,0) Two-dimensional semiconductors have potential to ease silicon integrated circuit challenges."];
  "N10" [label="(14,0,0) Metal oxides obtained from liquid-to-solid approach are versatile in category and function."];
  "N11" [label="(15,0,0) Solution-processed metal oxides as dielectrics in 2D devices remains an unexplored regime but offers possibilities if transferable."];
  "N12" [label="(16,0,0) We report a wet-chemistry-derived method to prepare amorphous CCTO which can be transferred into 2D devices."];
  "N13" [label="(17,0,0) CCTO/TMDs devices exhibit subthreshold swing of 67 mV dec-1 and ultra-small hysteresis, corroborating high-quality interface."];
  "N14" [label="(18,0,0) Utilizing optical properties of CCTO, optically writing and electrically erasing are achieved, leading to reconfigurable logic-in-sensor operation."];
  "N2" [label="(2,0,0) Performances of FETs and memory devices can be boosted by leveraging 2D semiconductors' characteristics."];
  "N3" [label="(4,0,0) The vdW surface of 2D semiconductors leads to a critical challenge in integrating high-quality dielectrics."];
  "N4" [label="(5,0,0) Absence of dangling bonds on 2D surfaces results in poor nucleation during direct deposition methods."];
  "N5" [label="(8,0,0) Using the transfer technique loosens restrictions in dielectric elements and synthesis temperatures."];
  "N6" [label="(10,0,0) The omnipresent nanogap between TMDs and transferred oxides suppresses gate leakage currents."];
  "N7" [label="(11,0,0) In all-in-one in-sensor computing, one layer is expected to be a sensing or multifunctional layer."];
  "N8" [label="(12,0,0) Deeply engineering the dielectric layer by rendering it multifunctional is worth exploring."];
  "N9" [label="(13,0,0) Traditional dielectrics prepared by gas-to-solid method are limited in material types and functions."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper investigates solution-processed freestanding amorphous copper calcium titanate films as transferable high-κ multifunctional dielectrics for van-der-Waals heterostructures with 2D transition-metal dichalcogenides, aiming to form a low-defect nanogap interface that yields near-ideal FET performance, including about 67 mV dec-1 subthreshold swing and ultra-small hysteresis, while enabling optically written and electrically erased floating-gate functionality for reconfigurable logic-in-sensor devices.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A transferable solution-processed dielectric platform that addresses vdW integration limits and exhibits both strong TMD FET metrics and optically written/electrically erased logic-in-sensor behavior motivates development and evaluation as a multifunctional dielectric for 2D vdW heterostructures."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) 2D semiconductors are promising for easing silicon integrated-circuit challenges and for improving FET and memory-device performance."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) The combined need for advanced 2D dielectric integration and the promise of wet-chemistry-derived oxides motivates targeting a transferable multifunctional solution-processed oxide dielectric strategy."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Wet-chemistry-derived amorphous CCTO is reported as a transferable oxide platform for testing this solution-processed dielectric strategy in 2D devices."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) CCTO/TMD devices demonstrate both optically written and electrically erased logic-in-sensor operation and strong FET-interface metrics, including 67 mV dec-1 subthreshold swing and ultra-small hysteresis corroborating a high-quality interface."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) Wet-chemistry-derived transferable amorphous CCTO is supported as a platform that combines 2D-device dielectric integration with high-quality CCTO/TMD FET behavior and optically written, electrically erased logic-in-sensor functionality."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) The promise of 2D semiconductors, together with the dielectric-integration bottleneck caused by vdW surfaces, motivates advanced dielectric-integration strategies for 2D semiconductor devices."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) For all-in-one in-sensor computing, multifunctional dielectric layers are worth exploring rather than established as strictly required."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Advanced dielectric-integration strategies for 2D semiconductors can reasonably include exploration of multifunctional dielectric integration for in-sensor computing."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Because transfer can enable high-quality dielectric integration, transferable solution-processed metal oxides are a motivated but still exploratory route for 2D-device dielectrics."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Transferable solution-processed oxides motivate exploration of functionally diverse dielectric candidates, given the functional versatility of wet-chemistry-derived metal oxides."];
  "N3" -> "I2" [label="deduction-case"];
